Review this CAP Node.js ticket handler. Only a transition to status='closed' must require the existing status to be 'open'; ordinary edits must still work. The service also has generic UPDATE handling. Show a concurrency-safe fix without causing a second update.
```js
this.before('UPDATE', Tickets, async req => {
  const ticket = await SELECT.one.from(Tickets).where({ ID: req.data.ID })
  if (ticket?.status !== 'open') return req.reject(409, 'Only open tickets can be closed')
})
```

