    throw new Error('Order must have at least one item')
  }
})
```
Explain the error-handling issue and give a supported replacement that rejects invalid writes but accepts nonempty items.

Review this CAP Java SDK 5.0 handler (linkedInterfaces=true, db is PersistenceService). The intent is to decrement stock when a submitOrder action is called, not on every CRUD update. Explain registration, key extraction, result typing, concurrency and failure/completion issues.
```java
@On(entity = Books_.class)
public void onOrderBook(CdsUpdateEventContext context) {
  String bookId = (String) context.getCqn().ref().segments().get(0).keys().get("ID");
  Result res = db.run(Select.from(Books_.class).where(b -> b.ID().eq(bookId)));
  Books book = res.single(Books.class);
  int newStock = book.getStock() - 1;
  db.run(Update.entity(Books_.class).where(b -> b.ID().eq(bookId)).data(Books.STOCK, newStock));
}
```

Review this CAP Java validation handler. Explain event/entity registration and supported business-error handling.
```java
@Before(event = CdsService.EVENT_CREATE, entity = Orders_.class)
public void validateOrder(List<Orders> orders) {
  for (Orders order : orders) {
    if (order.getItems() == null || order.getItems().isEmpty()) {
      throw new RuntimeException("Order must have at least one item");
    }
  }
}
```
Can the annotation attributes be omitted with this signature?

